  "notes": "Cash-basis county. Top-level receipts/disbursements, transfers and beginning balance come from the Statement of Cash Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p4, gained in the v8 re-trim; replaces the earlier Statement of Activities build, same totals). Beginning cash = Fund Balances - Beginning 6,599,710 (p4); ending cash = cash 6,762,441 + investments 11,002 (p1) = Fund Balances - Ending 6,773,443 (p4), also on the governmental funds cash basis assets statement (p3). Roll-forward ties: 6,599,710 + 9,996,155 - 9,822,422 + 3,501,863 - 3,501,863 = 6,773,443. Taxes 6,401,224 (p4) split: Inheritance 434,543 (p7) + Visitors Promotion lodging 6,802 (p14) + bond fund taxes 225,695 (pp17-18) + General Fund taxes 5,734,184 (p5, unlabeled type); sums to printed. Debt service principal 270,000 and interest 10,918 printed on p4. General Fund budgetary schedule (p5) prints TOTAL DISBURSEMENTS 5,232,136 while its lines add to 5,232,126 (5,232,126 also ties to the variance 527,084, excess 1,332,325 and the p4 General Fund column); the printed 5,232,136 is kept in detail_totals and the 10 difference is in report_discrepancies. Inheritance (3,061) and ARPA (7,695) disbursements are Public Works per the p4 fund columns. Nonmajor funds have more than 6 funds so the Total Nonmajor column is used in detail (budget schedules for nonmajor funds only show totals and are not duplicated). Statement of Activities transfers 3,501,836 vs fund statements 3,501,863 (see report_discrepancies). Balance sheet uses the government-wide Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1); p3 governmental funds statement matches it. Read pages 1-19 of 19"
